From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 10:23:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: remove only a recorded station BMC
 STA_REC

The removal of the BMC STA_REC on a zero BSSID does not check the
interface type. A mesh point always has a zero BSSID, and after a full
reset mac80211 reports the BSSID and the beacon enable together. The
driver then adds the mesh BMC STA_REC again and removes it at once, so
a mesh point loses that entry on every full reset. The removal also
goes to entries that do not exist.

Remove the entry only when the driver holds a station BSSID for it,
which only a station records when it adds the entry. A station still
removes its entry on disconnection, and mesh, AP and IBSS interfaces
keep theirs across a full reset.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/main.c |   10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -1101,15 +1101,15 @@ mt7996_link_info_changed(struct ieee8021
 	 * and then peer references bss_info_rfch to set bandwidth cap.
 	 */
 	if ((changed & BSS_CHANGED_BSSID && !is_zero_ether_addr(info->bssid)) ||
-	    (changed & BSS_CHANGED_BEACON_ENABLED))
+	    (changed & BSS_CHANGED_BEACON_ENABLED)) {
 		mt7996_vif_link_bss_add(phy, vif, info, link,
 					!!(changed & BSS_CHANGED_BSSID));
-	else if (changed & BSS_CHANGED_BSSID)
+	} else if (changed & BSS_CHANGED_BSSID &&
+		   !is_zero_ether_addr(link->bmc_bssid)) {
 		eth_zero_addr(link->bmc_bssid);
-
-	if (changed & BSS_CHANGED_BSSID && is_zero_ether_addr(info->bssid))
-		mt7996_mcu_add_sta(dev, info, NULL, link, &link->msta_link,
+		mt7996_mcu_add_sta(dev, info, NULL, link, NULL,
 				   CONN_STATE_DISCONNECT, false);
+	}
 
 	if (changed & BSS_CHANGED_HT || changed & BSS_CHANGED_ERP_CTS_PROT)
 		mt7996_mcu_set_protection(phy, link, info->ht_operation_mode,
